"The courier left on the third watch, alone, and Vance says he never logged her cargo," Mira reads aloud from the berth records. Dockmaster Vance Oduya shifts beside her but does not object. The logs show a dockhand named in the margin, and a berth number scratched out. Beneath the scratch-out, a heat signature burns on the sensor trace. It is a thin column of light that should not exist in a sealed bay. Out on the docking ring, Ren watches the corridor and counts the people who pass without looking at the bay. One of them walks too evenly. Vance clears his throat and says the berth was sealed before the courier ever arrived.

