You lean in the hatchway, one shoulder against the frame, and watch Vance Oduya's hands. They stay flat on the console, too flat, fingers spread as if holding the desk down. When Mira scrolls to the scratched-out berth, his thumb twitches once. He sees you noticing. His mouth tightens, and he reaches for the water flask at his belt without drinking from it. "Sealed means sealed," he says, a little loud. Behind you, the evenly walking stranger has stopped at the corridor's far end.

